<!--
  Authoritative source: the client certificate Apigee itself received during
  the two-way TLS handshake on its own VirtualHost, when mutual auth
  terminates at the gateway. tls.client.raw.cert/.s.dn/.i.dn are only
  populated when the VirtualHost has ClientAuthEnabled + a TrustStore
  configured (Edge Private/Public Cloud) or
  propagateTLSInformation.clientProperties = true (Apigee X/hybrid); that is
  environment/VirtualHost config outside this bundle, not something a
  SharedFlowBundle can set.

  Only reached (see sharedflows/default.xml's Condition) when
  tls.client.raw.cert is confirmed non-null, so it is safe to use <Template>
  here (which, unlike <Ref>, always produces a string, even ""; running it
  unconditionally would make client.cert.base64 resolve to "" instead of
  staying null when TLS gave us nothing, which would wrongly skip the header
  fallback below).

  client.cert.base64 strips tls.client.raw.cert's PEM armor and internal
  line-wrap whitespace down to bare base64, since that (not full PEM) is
  what gets embedded in the request to ISAM. replaceAll's regex is Apigee's
  message-template function (Java regex under the hood, confirmed against a
  Dino Chiesa Apigee-MessageTemplate-Demo example using the same
  {replaceAll(source,'pattern','replacement')} form), not JavaScript/Java
  code; no JavaCallout needed for this. The whitespace shorthand needs a
  DOUBLE backslash, \\s not \s: Apigee's own docs give \\s and \\d as the
  correct form for this argument position, since the argument string goes
  through the template engine's own escape processing before being handed
  to the regex compiler as \s; a single backslash was tried first and
  silently matched nothing (no compile error, just a no-op replace),
  exactly the symptom that showed up in testing.
-->
<AssignMessage name="AM-Extract-Client-Cert-TLS">
    <DisplayName>AM Extract Client Cert TLS</DisplayName>
    <AssignVariable>
        <Name>client.cert.base64</Name>
        <Template>{replaceAll(tls.client.raw.cert,'-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----|-----END CERTIFICATE-----|\\s','')}</Template>
    </AssignVariable>
    <AssignVariable>
        <Name>client.cert.subject.dn</Name>
        <Ref>tls.client.s.dn</Ref>
    </AssignVariable>
    <AssignVariable>
        <Name>client.cert.issuer.dn</Name>
        <Ref>tls.client.i.dn</Ref>
    </AssignVariable>
    <AssignVariable>
        <Name>client.cert.subject.dn.base64</Name>
        <Template>{encodeBase64(tls.client.s.dn)}</Template>
    </AssignVariable>
    <AssignVariable>
        <Name>client.cert.issuer.dn.base64</Name>
        <Template>{encodeBase64(tls.client.i.dn)}</Template>
    </AssignVariable>
    <IgnoreUnresolvedVariables>true</IgnoreUnresolvedVariables>
</AssignMessage>
